From: Waltteri Hooli <1420194+wahooli@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: codecs: aw88166: retry the start at prepare

The amp starts from DAPM PRE_PMU of its playback AIF, in a work item
that checks its PLL against the I2S clocks and retries five times in
quick succession. After system sleep ASoC powers DAPM back up before
userspace prepares the suspended stream again, so with a DSP back end
that stops its port for sleep the clocks are not running yet, the start
fails and nothing tries again.

Remember that DAPM has the playback path up, and start the amp again,
synchronously, from the DAI's prepare, which runs after the CPU DAI's
and so with the port running. With the amp already started it returns at
once. The same as the AW88261 needed on the AYANEO Pocket VERT; the AYN
Odin 3 has these.

While the card is still resuming (not back at D0), leave the start to
prepare. Otherwise the doomed attempt fails ("device start failed.
retry = 0") and reloads the DSP firmware over I2C on every resume, and
the first sound after waking waits for that.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/aw88166.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/aw88166.c
@@ -35,6 +35,7 @@
 	unsigned int re_init_val;
 	unsigned int dither_st;
 	bool phase_sync;
+	bool playback_pmu;
 };
 
 static const struct regmap_config aw88166_remap_config = {
@@ -1308,8 +1309,25 @@
 	dev_dbg(dai->dev, "shutdown stream=%d", substream->stream);
 }
 
+/*
+ * After system sleep DAPM powers the amp up before the stream is prepared
+ * again, so with the I2S port still stopped the PLL check fails. The CPU DAI
+ * is prepared first and starts the port: try again now.
+ */
+static int aw88166_prepare(struct snd_pcm_substream *substream, struct snd_soc_dai *dai)
+{
+	struct aw88166 *aw88166 = snd_soc_component_get_drvdata(dai->component);
+
+	guard(mutex)(&aw88166->lock);
+	if (aw88166->playback_pmu)
+		aw88166_start(aw88166, AW88166_SYNC_START);
+
+	return 0;
+}
+
 static const struct snd_soc_dai_ops aw88166_dai_ops = {
 	.startup = aw88166_startup,
+	.prepare = aw88166_prepare,
 	.set_fmt = aw88166_set_fmt,
 	.set_sysclk = aw88166_set_dai_sysclk,
 	.hw_params = aw88166_hw_params,
@@ -1701,9 +1719,13 @@
 	guard(mutex)(&aw88166->lock);
 	switch (event) {
 	case SND_SOC_DAPM_PRE_PMU:
-		aw88166_start(aw88166, AW88166_ASYNC_START);
+		aw88166->playback_pmu = true;
+		/* Still resuming: the port is stopped, so prepare starts the amp. */
+		if (snd_power_get_state(component->card->snd_card) == SNDRV_CTL_POWER_D0)
+			aw88166_start(aw88166, AW88166_ASYNC_START);
 		break;
 	case SND_SOC_DAPM_POST_PMD:
+		aw88166->playback_pmu = false;
 		aw88166_stop(aw88166->aw_pa);
 		break;
 	default:
